<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kyiv Pechersk Lavra</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1051</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> · Also known as Kiev Monastery of the Caves, Kiev Pechersk Lavra, Monastery of the Caves</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyiv">Kyiv</a> Pechersk Lavra, or Monastery of the Caves, is an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-orthodox-church">Orthodox</a> monastery in Kyiv founded in 1051 by the monks Anthony and Theodosius in caves above the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dnieper">Dnieper</a>. It became the leading monastery and centre of learning of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kievan-rus">Kievan Rus'</a>, where the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/primary-chronicle">Primary Chronicle</a> is traditionally thought to have been compiled, and its caves hold the relics of many monks venerated as saints. It is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco-world-heritage-site">UNESCO World Heritage Site</a>.</p></div>
